    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\tan3\\theta=\\dfrac{3\\tan\\theta-\\tan^3\\theta}{1-3\\tan^2\\theta}$.\n\nExpand $\\tan(2\\theta+\\theta)$, substitute the tangent double-angle formula and simplify the compound fraction.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan3\\theta&=\\tan(2\\theta+\\theta)\\\\\\tan3\\theta&=\\frac{\\tan2\\theta+\\tan\\theta}{1-\\tan2\\theta\\tan\\theta}\\\\\\tan3\\theta&=\\frac{\\dfrac{2\\tan\\theta}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}+\\tan\\theta}{1-\\dfrac{2\\tan^2\\theta}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}}\\\\\\tan3\\theta&=\\frac{2\\tan\\theta+\\tan\\theta(1-\\tan^2\\theta)}{1-\\tan^2\\theta-2\\tan^2\\theta}\\\\\\tan3\\theta&=\\frac{3\\tan\\theta-\\tan^3\\theta}{1-3\\tan^2\\theta}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
